---
// The two halves of the trade, drawn from a shared zero so they oppose each
// other: what the compression meter says it saved, and what the destroyed cache
// discount cost. The third row is the residual, which is the point.
const SPAN = 19; // dollars either side of zero
const x = (v) => 50 + (v / SPAN) * 50;
const rows = [
  { name: 'compression saving, as metered', v: 15.41, cls: 'blue' },
  { name: 'cache discount destroyed',       v: -16.37, cls: 'warm' },
  { name: 'net',                            v: -0.96, cls: 'warm' },
];
const money = (v) => (v < 0 ? '-$' : '+$') + Math.abs(v).toFixed(2);
const pitch = 46;
---
<figure class="fig">
  <p class="fig-head">what compression saved, against what it destroyed</p>
  <p class="fig-sub">dollars across the 25-task on-token arm</p>
  <svg height="156" role="img" aria-labelledby="cc-t cc-d">
    <title id="cc-t">The $15.41 of metered compression savings is cancelled by $16.37 of lost cache discount, leaving a net of minus $0.96.</title>
    <desc id="cc-d">Two bars of nearly equal length pointing in opposite directions from zero, and a third bar showing the residual, which is a sliver 17 times shorter than either.</desc>
    <line class="zero" x1="50%" x2="50%" y1="6" y2="134.5" />
    {rows.map((r, i) => {
      const lo = r.v < 0 ? x(r.v) : 50;
      const w = Math.abs(x(r.v) - 50);
      return (
        <g>
          <rect class="knock" x="0" y={2 + i * pitch} width="100%" height="17" />
          <text class="t-name" x="0" y={14 + i * pitch}>{r.name}</text>
          <text class="t-val" x="100%" y={14 + i * pitch} text-anchor="end">{money(r.v)}</text>
          <rect class={`m-${r.cls}`} x={`${lo}%`} y={20 + i * pitch} width={`${w}%`} height="12" rx="4" />
          {r.v < 0
            ? <g transform="translate(-4,0)"><rect class={`m-${r.cls}`} x="50%" y={20 + i * pitch} width="4" height="12" /></g>
            : <rect class={`m-${r.cls}`} x="50%" y={20 + i * pitch} width="4" height="12" />}
        </g>
      );
    })}
    <line class="grid" x1="0" x2="100%" y1="134.5" y2="134.5" />
    <text class="t-ax" x="10.526%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">-$15</text>
    <text class="t-ax" x="50%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">$0</text>
    <text class="t-ax" x="89.474%" y="150" text-anchor="middle">+$15</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    Token mode busted the provider cache <b>123</b> times against the control's <b>14</b>, and cache-read
    reuse per write token fell from <b>38:1</b> to <b>11:1</b>. That knocked <b>6,062,098</b> tokens out of
    the cache and into full-price billing, worth $16.37 of forfeited discount, against $15.41 of savings
    headroom credited itself.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
